NON-RESULT, cycle 64 material #3, 2026-09-21 13:1x-13:2x. This file held NO measurement.

It was the log of a WAIT LOOP (a python one-liner polling the peer dispatch's log until it carried an end
marker) and of one killed placeholder before it. Its own COMMAND LINE quoted the end-marker strings it was
searching for, and bgrun echoes the command line into the log - so tools/hooks/guard_peer.py's FAILURE_RE
matched the waiter's own search pattern and the file became "the newest failing log", blocking the batch it
was waiting for. No LabVIEW object was touched by either process, nothing was built, nothing was measured.

The content is rewritten here (rather than the file being deleted) so the event stays on the record. The
lesson, for whoever writes the next waiter: never put the strings `BGRUN` + `END` / `TIMEOUT` (or any other
FAILURE_RE token) on the command line of a job whose output bgrun logs under tools/bench/ - poll from a
file that is not a bench log, or match the marker by a split literal.
